Error: Jet.ReturnTypeMismatch: This value is [Int], but `firsts` returns `Grid<Int>` (which is [[Int]])
  --> Tests/UI/alias_shows_source_name_and_expansion.jet:5:29
    |
  5 | firsts: fn() -> Grid<Int> { [Int]{1} }
    |                             ^^^^^^^^
 Why: `firsts` declares [[Int]] as its result, so the value it hands back must be [[Int]]
 Fix: Wrap the value in a list: `[value]`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ReturnTypeMismatch

Error: Jet.ValueTypeMismatch: `total` wants `Grid<Int>` (which is [[Int]]) for argument 1, but this is [Int]
  --> Tests/UI/alias_shows_source_name_and_expansion.jet:7:25
    |
  7 | run: fn() { print(total([Int]{1, 2})) }
    |                         ^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Every argument must match its parameter's type
 Fix: Use [[Int]] here
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ValueTypeMismatch

Error: Jet.ReturnTypeMismatch: This value is [Int], but `pairs_of` returns `Pairs<Int>` (which is [(Int, Int)])
  --> Tests/UI/alias_shows_source_name_and_expansion.jet:13:32
    |
 13 | pairs_of: fn() -> Pairs<Int> { [Int]{1} }
    |                                ^^^^^^^^
 Why: `pairs_of` declares [(Int, Int)] as its result, so the value it hands back must be [(Int, Int)]
 Fix: Hand back a [(Int, Int)] value: convert this value to [(Int, Int)], or return the value you meant
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ReturnTypeMismatch

